Licensing Notice
================

This repository contains (1) components adapted from HydroDL and (2) original
research code developed for nitrate gap-reconstruction experiments.

HydroDL-derived components
--------------------------
The following files under Models/LSTM_SplitTest/ are adapted from HydroDL
(https://github.com/mhpi/hydroDL), developed by the Multi-scale Hydrology,
Processes and Intelligence (MHPI) research group at The Pennsylvania State
University:

  - model.py
  - dropout.py
  - train_functions.py

Those components (and modifications thereof) are redistributed under the
HydroDL Non-Commercial Software License Agreement. The complete, unmodified
license text is in:

  THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES/hydroDL-LICENSE.txt

Commercial use of HydroDL-derived code requires prior written consent from
The Pennsylvania State University (see that license).

Original contributions
----------------------
All other source code in this repository — including gap-generation
workflows, regional/signature donor selection, data preprocessing, evaluation
procedures, and experiment orchestration — was developed for this research
project.

A final permissive license (for example BSD 3-Clause) for those original
components has not been applied as a blanket repository license, because it
would conflict with HydroDL's non-commercial terms for the adapted files.
Confirm the licensing of original contributions with your advisor and/or the
Penn State Open Source Program Office before treating this repository as the
official WRR manuscript code archive.

Until that decision is recorded here, original contributions are provided for
non-commercial research use consistent with the accompanying manuscript, with
all rights reserved by the copyright holders except as required by the
HydroDL license for the adapted components above.

See README.md ("Code Attribution and Licensing") for a short summary.
